{
  "id": "DrugBank_DB00885 - MONDO_5642",
  "verbalization": "Pemirolast is implicated in the pathogenesis of Atopic Conjunctivitis through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of Papillary Conjunctivitis. The drug's indication for Papillary Conjunctivitis is linked to two other conditions, Tromethamine and Levocabastine, which in turn are linked to Atopic Conjunctivitis. This suggests that Pemirolast may exert its effects on the conjunctival tissue by targeting Papillary Conjunctivitis, potentially through mechanisms that reduce inflammation or modulate immune responses. The shared pathway from Pemirolast to Papillary Conjunctivitis and then to Atopic Conjunctivitis indicates a possible mechanistic link, though the exact nature of the interaction remains unclear. The evidence supports a potential role for Pemirolast in the management of Atopic Conjunctivitis through a chain of indications, but further research is needed to elucidate the precise mechanism of action.",
